,"github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3932#issuecomment-566055434"},"message":"It would be critical to know what was in the directory beforehand. `create --force` is a standard thing to run, and should not exhibit this behavior, nor should users have to manually perform `annex init`. Can you somehow replicate this?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"88f83e30129b333b75d75bb6fcd824ef7032aa1f"},"timestamp":1576503401,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NjA2MzAxNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3932#issuecomment-566063016"},"message":"I've tried it again on a different folder (both an empty folder and one that needed `create --force`), as well as on the existing folder after removing the `.git`, `.gitattributes` and `.datalad` folders/files and couldn't replicate the error message that way.\n\nHowever, going a bit further back I have tried to use `datalad create --force` on the same folder from a different server (that had access to the files but wasn't hosting them) giving me the following error:\n\n\u003e user@differentserver:/path/to/data$ datalad create --force\n\u003e [INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /path/to/data \n\u003e [INFO   ] error: file write error: Bad file descriptor \n\u003e [INFO   ] fatal: unable to write sha1 file \n\u003e [INFO   ] error: file write error: Bad file descriptor \n\u003e [INFO   ] fatal: unable to write sha1 file \n\u003e [INFO   ] git-annex: failed to read sha from git write-tree \n\u003e [INFO   ] CallStack (from HasCallStack): \n\u003e [INFO   ]   error, called at ./Git/Sha.hs:18:15 in main:Git.Sha \n\u003e [INFO   ] git-annex: init: 1 failed \n\u003e CommandError: command '['git-annex', 'init']' failed with exitcode 1\n\u003e Failed to run ['git-annex', 'init'] under '/path/to/data'. Exit code=1.\n\u003e init  \n\u003e failed\n\nI can recreate the original error if I run `datalad create --force` first on the other server resulting in that error message, and then