 'create', '--force'] \n[DEBUG  ] Determined class of decorated function: \u003cclass 'datalad.core.local.create.Create'\u003e \n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /data/BnB_TEMP/this \n[DEBUG  ] Setting annex backend to MD5E (persistently) \n[DEBUG  ] \u003cAnnexRepo path=/data/BnB_TEMP/this (\u003cclass 'datalad.support.annexrepo.AnnexRepo'\u003e)\u003e.get_content_info(...) \n[DEBUG  ] Query repo: ['git', 'ls-files', '--stage', '-z', '-d', '-m', '--exclude-standard', '-o'] \n[DEBUG  ] Done query repo: ['git', 'ls-files', '--stage', '-z', '-d', '-m', '--exclude-standard', '-o'] \n[DEBUG  ] Done \u003cAnnexRepo path=/data/BnB_TEMP/this (\u003cclass 'datalad.support.annexrepo.AnnexRepo'\u003e)\u003e.get_content_info(...) \n[DEBUG  ] 2 path(s) to add to \u003cAnnexRepo path=/data/BnB_TEMP/this (\u003cclass 'datalad.support.annexrepo.AnnexRepo'\u003e)\u003e {'.gitattributes': {'type': 'file', 'state': 'untracked'}, '.datalad': {'type': 'directory', 'state': 'untracked'}} \n[DEBUG  ] Committing via direct call of git: ['git', 'commit', '-m', '[DATALAD] new dataset'] \nCommandError: command '['git', 'commit', '-m', '[DATALAD] new dataset', '--', '.gitattributes', '.datalad']' failed with exitcode 1\nFailed to run ['git', 'commit', '-m', '[DATALAD] new dataset', '--', '.gitattributes', '.datalad'] under '/data/BnB_TEMP/this'. Exit code=1. out= err=fatal: cannot exec '.git/hooks/pre-commit': Text file busy\n\nfatal: cannot exec '.git/hooks/pre-commit': Text file busy\n```\n\nI think the error message are sensible and enable recovery for the unfortunate user of such a system ;-)\n\nI don't think it is datalad's duty to sort out half-broken Git repos, or anticipate their presence. I am therefore closing this issue. Feel free to reopen, if you disagree and have a suggestion what other action should be taken.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1576505714,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50Mjg4NjExMTY3N